        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_BEDNETS_TWO",
            "message": "For the planned line, the cumulative 'Quantity distributed' for the assigned boundary is used, and for the actual line, the 'Quantity distributed' for the date range is used. To calculate the X-intercept, the bed nets targeted to distribute per day for assigned boundary or district is multiplied by the number of days in the date range (Campaign start date - TODAY). Finally, the interval for the x-axis is kept for every 1 day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress (Household)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_FIVE",
            "message": "The interval for the X-axis is kept for every 1 day, meaning that each point on the chart represents the progress made in one day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_FOUR",
            "message": "To calculate the X-intercept of the “planned” line, the number of households targeted to visit per day for the assigned boundary is multiplied by the number of days in the date range (Campaign start date - TODAY). For the X-intercept of the “actual” line, the current date is added to the difference between the target number of households and the total number of households visited to date, divided by the number of households targeted per day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_ONE",
            "message": "This chart is used to track the planned versus actual progress of a campaign to deliver household visits, and to project when the campaign will reach its target. The chart is a line chart with two lines: one for the planned progress and one for the actual progress.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_THREE",
            "message": "The “actual” line represents the actual number of households that were visited each day, starting from the beginning of the campaign up to the current day. The total number of households visited for each day is used to plot this line. The X-intercept of the actual line shows the projected date when the campaign is expected to meet its target, based on the current rate of progress.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_HOUSEHOLD_TWO",
            "message": "The “planned” line represents the expected number of households that should have been visited each day, based on the micro plan. The cumulative number of households that were targeted to visit each day is used to plot this line. The X-intercept of the planned line shows the date when the campaign is expected to meet its target.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION",
            "message": "Planned vs Actual Campaign Progress (Population)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_FIVE",
            "message": "The x-axis interval is set to 1 day, meaning that each point on the chart represents the progress made in one day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_FOUR",
            "message": "The calculation of the intercept is done by dividing the difference between the target population and the actual population covered by the population targeted per day and adding the result to today's date.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_ONE",
            "message": "This is a line chart that compares the planned and actual campaign progression for population coverage.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_THREE",
            "message": "The actual data is obtained from the quantity distributed for a given date range. The X-intercept on the chart indicates when the population target is expected to be met based on the current rate of coverage.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_PLANNED_VS_ACTUAL_PROGRESS_POPULATION_TWO",
            "message": "Planned data is calculated by adding up the cumulative quantity delivered and multiplying it by a factor of 1.8, representing the average population per household.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_POPULATION_COVERED",
            "message": "Population Covered",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_POPULATION_COVERED_ONE",
            "message": "This KPI visualization in the “Registration and Delivery” dashboard section displays the total population covered within the selected date range. This data is sourced from the application's delivery intervention screen where the quantity of bed nets delivered is recorded. The boundary data used for this section is MDMS.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_POPULATION_COVERED_THREE",
            "message": "For the \"%\" toggle, the data is presented as a percentage of the total population covered, calculated by summing the number of individuals covered in each household and multiplying it by 100, and then dividing it by the daily population microplan target and the number of days in the selected date range. The data is presented separately for each boundary, which could be districts for national and provincial roles, and Administrative posts for district roles.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_POPULATION_COVERED_TWO",
            "message": "For the \"Number\" toggle, the data is presented as a sum of all households visited within the selected date range. The data is presented separately for each boundary, which could be districts for national and provincial roles, and Administrative posts for district roles.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT",
            "message": "Summary Report",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY",
            "message": "Summary Report (Boundary)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_FOUR",
            "message": "The report allows for drill-down functionality, allowing users to view data at a more granular level for each boundary. The Target Achievement columns show the percentage of micro plan targets achieved for household coverage, population coverage, and bed nets distribution.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_ONE",
            "message": "The summary report provides an overview of the progress of the campaign in different boundaries such as district, administrative post, for different metrics such as household coverage, population coverage, and bed nets distribution.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_THREE",
            "message": "Additionally, it provides data on the number of households where no delivery has taken place and the reasons for the non-delivery.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_BOUNDARY_TWO",
            "message": "The report also includes information on the total number of households visited, the total population covered, and the total bed nets distributed for the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAY",
            "message": "Summary Report (Day)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAY_ONE",
            "message": "The summary table provides an overview of the campaign progress for each day. The table shows the date, target achievement percentage for households, population, and bed nets distribution, the total number of households visited, the total population covered, the total number of bed nets distributed, and the total number of households where no delivery has taken place along with the reasons.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_SUMMARY_REPORT_DAY_TWO",
            "message": "The table does not allow drilling down on the dates, and the last row of each column represents the sum of all data above it. This report helps to monitor the progress of the campaign, and it provides a daily summary of the achievements and challenges faced during the campaign.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_FIVE",
            "message": "District Level User: He is able to view the data for the respective district that he has been assigned.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_FOUR",
            "message": "Province Level User: He is able to view the data for the respective province he has been assigned.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TAB_OVERVIEW_THREE",
            "message": "National Level User : He is able to view the data for the selected province.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT",
            "message": "Target Achievement",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS",
            "message": "Target Achievement (Bed nets)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS_FIVE",
            "message": "Insights are also available, with the percentage change in coverage between the current day and the previous day indicated.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS_FOUR",
            "message": "The formula used to calculate the coverage percentage is the sum of the bed nets distributed in each AP divided by the bed nets micro plan target for that AP.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS_ONE",
            "message": "The heat map metric measures the distribution coverage of bed nets achieved against micro plan targets across different districts. The micro plan targets are set up during the project setup phase, and the bed nets distributed are recorded in the Delivery Intervention screen in the mobile application under the Quantity Distributed field.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS_THREE",
            "message": "For district-level users, the default view of the heat map is at the assigned district level, with the bed nets distribution coverage indicated as a percentage for each administrative post (AP) within the district. However, since shapefiles are not available at the AP level, the view will have only the district outer boundary and not AP boundaries within it.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_BEDNETS_TWO",
            "message": "For national and provincial level users, the default view of the heat map is at the province level, with the bed nets distribution coverage indicated as a percentage for each district. The formula used to calculate the coverage percentage is the sum of the bed nets distributed in each district divided by the bed nets micro plan target for that district.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD",
            "message": "Target Achievement (Household)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD_FIVE",
            "message": "Finally, due to the unavailability of shapefiles beyond the district level, zooming in beyond the district level is not possible, and therefore, the map will only show the outer boundary of the district or administrative post.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD_FOUR",
            "message": "The metric also provides an insight that compares the household coverage between two days, expressed as a percentage change.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD_ONE",
            "message": "The Target Achievement of Households shows the geo map with percentage of households covered against the micro plan targets set for a particular district or administrative post. The micro plan targets are set at the project setup stage, and the household coverage is based on data fetched from the mobile application, which shows the households that have been visited. The metric is presented as a heat map that visualizes the percentage of household coverage achieved across different districts.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD_THREE",
            "message": "For district-level users, the default view of the map is at the district level, and the metric is calculated as follows: Total households visited till today in an administrative post (AP) divided by the Household Micro plan target set for that AP multiplied by 100. The same calculation is performed for each AP within the district.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_HOUSEHOLD_TWO",
            "message": "For national and provincial users, the default view of the map is at the province level, and the metric is calculated as follows: Total households visited till today in a district divided by the Household Micro plan target set for that district multiplied by 100. The same calculation is performed for each district within the province.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION",
            "message": "Target Achievement (Population)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_FIVE",
            "message": "Insights will be available in terms of percentage change in coverage between today and the previous day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_FOUR",
            "message": "However, due to the unavailability of shapefiles beyond the district level, there will be no zoom-in available for both national/provincial and district-level users.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_ONE",
            "message": "This metric measures the population coverage achieved against the micro plan targets in percentage. It will be presented as a heat map that shows the coverage percentage across different districts.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_SIX",
            "message": "It is important to note that for district-level users, the view will only show the district outer boundary, as the shapefiles for administrative posts are not available.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_THREE",
            "message": "For national and provincial level users, the default view will be at the province level, with the coverage percentage calculated as the sum of the population data covered in each district divided by the population micro plan target of that district, multiplied by 100. The same formula will be used for district-level users, with the default view set at the district level.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_REGISTRATION_AND_DELIVERY_TARGET_ACHIEVEMENT_POPULATION_TWO",
            "message": "The micro plan targets and boundary data are provided in the project setup, while the bed nets distributed and population data covered are obtained from the delivery intervention screen in the application. The population data covered is calculated as the quantity distributed multiplied by 1.8, which is the average number of people per household in the country.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS",
            "message": "Summary Report (Open complaints)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY",
            "message": "Boundary",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_ONE",
            "message": "This metric of the tabular chart displays the different boundaries for which the open complaints data count is reported. The boundary data will be as per the user role. I.e. ‘National’ and ‘provincial’ level users will get district level boundary data, whereas ‘district’ level users will get administrative post level boundary data. The drill-down functionality will be available for all levels of boundaries.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_ONE",
            "message": "The Summary Report for Open Complaints is a tabular chart that shows the overview of complaints that are open from a particular duration with respect to the boundary. The report is categorized according to different boundaries within MDMS, and the complaints data is sourced for the “Open”, Complaints data module in the mobile application. The report allows for drill-down capabilities from one level of boundary to the last.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS",
            "message": "Open since > 48 hrs",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS_ONE",
            "message": "This report shows the total number of open complaints for a particular boundary where the complaints have been open for more than 48 hours during the selected date range. The report calculates this by summing all the complaints where the status is \"Open\" and the time between the created time and 23:59 hours on selected end Date is more than 48 hours.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS_TWO",
            "message": "The total number of open complaints is calculated by subtracting the sum of rejected and resolved complaints from the total number of complaints. The boundary for users can be a district for National & Provincial supervisors, and Administrative post for District supervisors. The last row of the column should be the sum of all columns above, which represents the total number of open complaints for more than 48 hours in the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_HOURS",
            "message": "Open since < 6 hrs ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_HOURS_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Open since < 6 Hours\" summary report shows the total number of open complaints that are less than 6 hours old for the selected date range. The calculation for this report involves summing up all complaints where the status is \"Open\" and the complaint was created within the selected date range. In addition to this, the complaint must also have been created within 6 hours of the end of the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_HOURS_TWO",
            "message": "The last row of the column shows the total sum of all columns above. This report helps supervisors to quickly identify newly registered complaints that need to be addressed urgently.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_TO_TWELVE_HOURS",
            "message": "Open since > 6 hrs & <12 hrs ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_TO_TWELVE_HOURS_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Open since > 6 hrs & <12 hrs\" column in the summary report shows the total number of open complaints for the selected date range that have been open for more than 6 hours but less than 12 hours. The calculation is based on the time difference between the created time of the complaint and the end of the day on the specified date, which should fall between 6 and 12 hours.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_SIX_TO_TWELVE_HOURS_TWO",
            "message": "The total number of open complaints for a given boundary (i.e., district or province) is calculated by summing all the complaints in that boundary that have the \"OPEN\" status and were created within the selected date range. This number is then further filtered to include only those complaints that have been open for more than 6 hours but less than 12 hours. The last row of the column shows the sum of all the values in that column for each boundary.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWELVE_TO_TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS",
            "message": "Open since > 12 hrs & <24 hrs ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWELVE_TO_TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Open since > 12 hours & <24 hours\" section of the report shows the total number of open complaints that have been open for more than 12 hours but less than 24 hours, for a particular boundary within the selected date range. This is calculated by adding up all the complaints with the status of \"OPEN\" that were created within the boundary and have been open for more than 12 hours but less than 24 hours. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWELVE_TO_TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS_TWO",
            "message": "The open complaints are determined by subtracting the sum of \"Resolved\" and \"Rejected” complaints from the total complaints created for the boundary. The boundary is for which the data is being displayed, which can be District or Provincial, depending on the user role assigned. The last row of the column shows the sum of all the complaints in the column.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWENTY_FOUR_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS",
            "message": "Open since > 24 hrs & < 48 hrs ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWENTY_FOUR_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS_ONE",
            "message": "This report shows the total number of complaints that are still open and have not been resolved within the specified time frame, which is between 24 to 48 hours. The calculation is based on the time difference between the complaint creation time and the end of the day on the selected date. The data is filtered by the boundary of districts for national and provincial supervisors, and Administrative Posts for district supervisors.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_OPEN_SINCE_TWENTY_FOUR_FOURTY_EIGHT_HOURS_TWO",
            "message": "The open complaints are calculated as the difference between the total complaints and the resolved and rejected complaints. The last row of the column is the sum of all the values in the respective columns. This report helps supervisors to monitor the number of open complaints that have not been resolved within the specified time frame.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_OPEN_COMPLAINTS_TWO",
            "message": "If a date range is selected, the end date will default to today's date. The report will display the total number of open complaints for each boundary, with the last row of the column showing the sum of all columns. In summary, the Summary Report for Open Complaints provides a quick overview of the number of complaints that are still open within a selected duration and allows users to drill down to different levels of boundaries to get more granular information.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS",
            "message": "Summary Report (Total complaints)",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE",
            "message": "Summary Report  (Total Complaints ) : ‘Boundary’ Toggle",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_BOUNDARY",
            "message": "Boundary",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_BOUNDARY_ONE",
            "message": "This metric of the tabular chart displays the different boundaries for which the complaints data is reported. The boundary data will be as per the user role. I.e. ‘National’ and ‘provincial’ level users will get district level boundary data, whereas ‘district’ level users will get administrative post level boundary data. The drill-down functionality will be available for all levels of boundaries.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_ONE",
            "message": "The summary report for total complaints will be presented in a tabular chart format, which will provide an overview of the total complaints according to the boundary. Each boundary will be clickable and will allow drilling down to the next level of boundary for detailed information. The boundary data will be taken from the MDMS, and complaints data will be from the complaints module in the mobile application.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_OPEN",
            "message": "Open",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_OPEN_ONE",
            "message": "The ‘Open’ Complaints in the summary report refers to the total number of complaints that are currently open and have not yet been resolved or rejected. All the complaints which do not have the status as Resolved or Rejected are termed as open; else to whatever state/status they are in. This means that no action has been taken on these complaints, and they are still waiting for attention from the relevant authorities. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_OPEN_THREE",
            "message": "Finally, the report provides a total row at the bottom that sums up all the open complaints for all the boundaries. This information is helpful in identifying the workload and the current state of the complaint handling process.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_OPEN_TWO",
            "message": "The report calculates this number by summing up all the complaints in the selected boundary where the status is marked as \"Open\" and the date range is within the selected range. The report distinguishes between the different levels of authorities, such as National, Provincial, or District supervisors, and shows the total number of open complaints for each one accordingly. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED",
            "message": "Registered",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED_ONE",
            "message": "This provides information about the total number of complaints registered for the selected date range for each boundary level. The calculation for the \"Total Complaints Registered\" is the sum of all complaints that were created for the selected date range for each boundary level.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED_TWO",
            "message": "This includes complaints that are open, resolved, and rejected. The last row of the column should be equal to the sum of all the columns above it, providing the total number of complaints registered across all boundary levels.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REJECTED",
            "message": "Rejected By Supervisor",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REJECTED_ONE",
            "message": "This the total number of complaints that were rejected by a supervisor for the selected date range. The data field in the report shows the total number of complaints rejected for each boundary. Further the boundaries displayed depend on the user role, with national and provincial level users seeing districts as the default boundary data, while district level users see administrative posts as the default boundary data. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REJECTED_THREE",
            "message": "The last row of the \"Rejected by Supervisor\" column shows the sum of all columns above it, indicating the total number of complaints rejected for all boundaries.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_REJECTED_TWO",
            "message": "The drill-down feature is available for all boundaries, till the last village level. To calculate the total number of complaints rejected for each boundary, the system sums up all the complaints where the status is marked as \"Rejected\" and where the boundary is equal to different districts or administrative posts as applicable by user role and the date range is the one selected by the user. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED",
            "message": "Resolved",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED_ONE",
            "message": "The purpose of the section is to show the total number of complaints that were resolved within the selected date range for each boundary. This displays the data for each boundary, which could be district or administrative posts depending on the user's role. The calculation for the number of resolved complaints involves adding up all the complaints where the status is marked as \"RESOLVED\" for a given boundary and date range. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_BOUNDARY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED_TWO",
            "message": "The last row of the \"Resolved\" column shows the sum of all the resolved complaints for each boundary, giving an overall count of the number of complaints resolved for the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE",
            "message": "Summary Report  (Total Complaints ) : ‘Day’ Toggle",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_DATE",
            "message": "Date",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_DATE_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Date\" column in the summary report with \"Day\" toggle shows the complaint data according to the date. The default view is the starting date of the campaign. and there is no drill-down available for the dates.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_ONE",
            "message": "The Summary Report with 'Day' Toggle displays a tabular chart that shows data for each day of the campaign, with no drill down on the dates. The report shows Complaint data as per the date, with Boundary data coming from MDMS and Complaint data from the Complaints module in the mobile application. The last row of each column will be the total sum of all columns. The Date Report does not have any change as per the date range selected. The Report will be from the Campaign start date till today.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_OPEN",
            "message": "Open",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_OPEN_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Open\" column in the Day toggle chart shows the total number of complaints on a particular day for which no action has been taken yet and the status is not Rejected or Resolved. Using the three metrics (Total Complaints: / Rejected / Resolved), the number of open complaints can be calculated by subtracting the total number of resolved and rejected complaints from the total number of complaints created on a particular day.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_OPEN_TWO",
            "message": "The last row of the column shows the sum of all open complaints. The Day toggle chart data is not affected by the date range selection.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED",
            "message": "Registered",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED_ONE",
            "message": "The summary of Registered complaints shows the total number of complaints that have been registered on each day. The total complaints registered for a particular date is calculated by summing up all the complaints that have been created on that date for the user boundary allotted. The boundary data is determined by the user's role. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REGISTERED_TWO",
            "message": "National and provincial supervisors will have the default boundary data set to the district, whereas district supervisors will have administrative posts as the default boundary data. The total number of complaints is calculated as the sum of all complaints that are currently open, resolved, or rejected.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REJECTED",
            "message": "Rejected By Supervisor",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REJECTED_ONE",
            "message": "The \"Rejected by Supervisor\" column in the Day toggle chart displays the total number of complaints that were rejected by the supervisor for each date. This is calculated as the difference between \"Total Complaints Registered\" and the sum of open and resolved complaints.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_REJECTED_TWO",
            "message": "The last row of the column shows the total number of complaints that were rejected by the supervisor, across all dates. It should be noted that the Day toggle chart is not affected by the date range selection, and always displays data for each day of the campaign.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED",
            "message": "Resolved",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED_ONE",
            "message": "This section in the summary report for ‘Day’ toggle shows the total number of complaints that were resolved on each date. This is calculated by summing up all the complaints that have a status of \"RESOLVED\" for the corresponding date and boundary (i.e., \"Province\" for Provincial and National supervisors and \"District\" for District supervisors).",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUMMARY_REPORT_TOTAL_COMPLAINTS_DAY_TOGGLE_RESOLVED_TWO",
            "message": "The last row of the \"Resolved\" column is the sum of all the resolved complaints for all the dates. The Day toggle chart is not affected by the DATE RANGE selection, which means that the chart will show data for each day of the campaign regardless of the selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DATA_SYNC",
            "message": "Data Sync",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DATA_SYNC_ONE",
            "message": "Data Sync rate refers to the percentage of users who have synced their device with the application at least once for a specified time period. It is calculated as the total number of users who have synced their device divided by the total number of users created, expressed as a percentage.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DATA_SYNC_THREE",
            "message": "The drill-down for this information is limited to the Administrative Post level. This means that for National/Provincial supervisors, the drill-down will be from \"District\" to \"Administrative Post\". For District supervisors, the information will directly display the Administrative Post without the need for drill-down.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DATA_SYNC_TWO",
            "message": "In addition, the percentage of users who have synced their device at least once for the selected day will be displayed. This information will be displayed in the form of a bar chart, with the x-axis showing the different boundaries as per the user role who is viewing, and the y-axis showing the percentage of users who have synced their device in that boundary.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DISTRICT_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE",
            "message": "District Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DISTRICT_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_ONE",
            "message": "The District Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate is a bar chart that shows the percentage completion of checklists allotted and to be filled by district-level supervisors. The data for this feature is taken from the supervisor module in the application, specifically for checklists completion. The level of the supervisor is retrieved from the user management module.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DISTRICT_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_POINT_ONE",
            "message": "For ‘National/Provincial Supervisors’ the number of entries is calculated by counting the number of checklists created within the selected/assigned province and selected date range, where the supervisor level is District and the number of checklists available and assigned.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DISTRICT_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_POINT_TWO",
            "message": "For ‘District Supervisors’ the number of entries is calculated by counting the number of checklists created within the assigned district and selected date range, where the supervisor level is District and the different checklists available for him and assigned.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_DISTRICT_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_TWO",
            "message": "The calculation for the chart is as follows:",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_NATIONAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE",
            "message": "National Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_NATIONAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_FOUR",
            "message": "The result is presented as a bar chart that displays the percentage completion of checklists by national-level supervisors. This metric provides an overview of how national-level supervisors are performing in terms of completing the checklists assigned to them, and it helps in identifying areas where further attention is required to ensure that the checklists are completed on time.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_NATIONAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_ONE",
            "message": "The ‘National Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate’ is a metric displayed as a bar chart in the dashboard section. This metric measures the percentage completion of checklists by national-level supervisors. The data is derived from the supervisor application, user management module, and the frequency of checklist completion.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_NATIONAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_THREE",
            "message": "For ‘national/provincial supervisors’, the number of entries is calculated where supervisor level is national and checklists are the different checklists available to be filled. For ‘district supervisors’, the number of entries is calculated where supervisor level is national and checklists are different checklists available to be filled at the district level.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_NATIONAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_TWO",
            "message": "To calculate this metric, the application requires input fields such as the level of supervisor, frequency of checklist completion, and the number of checklists created within the selected/assigned province or district and selected date range.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE",
            "message": "Provincial Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_FIVE",
            "message": "The level of the supervisor is obtained from the user management module, and the frequency of checklist completion is also considered in the calculation. For national/provincial supervisors, the number of entries is calculated for the selected/assigned province and the checklist name, whereas for district supervisors, the number of entries is calculated for the assigned district and checklist name.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_FOUR",
            "message": "The data required for the calculation of this metric is obtained from the supervisor application/module, which is used for checklists completion. ",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_ONE",
            "message": "Provincial Supervisors Checklists Completion Rate is a metric that shows the percentage completion of checklists by provincial-level supervisors. This bar chart is displayed in the dashboard, and helps to monitor the performance of the checklist that has been filled and submitted by provincial-level supervisors.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_THREE",
            "message": "This calculation is performed for each checklist assigned to the provincial-level supervisors, and the results are displayed in a bar chart format.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISORS_CHECKLIST_COMPLETION_RATE_TWO",
            "message": "To calculate this metric, the number of checklists created for provincial-level supervisors to be filled, for the selected/assigned province and selected date range is counted, and the number of checklists completed is calculated. The completed checklists are then divided by the total number of checklists created, and this ratio is multiplied by 100 to get the percentage completion rate.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_TAB_OVERVIEW_ONE",
            "message": "The ‘Supervisor’ section in the dashboard provides a visual representation of the actions taken by supervisors on the activities / checklist assigned to them. This section shows the response of all three levels of users: National, Provincial, and District.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_TAB_OVERVIEW_THREE",
            "message": "This information can be used by higher-level management to monitor the progress of activities and identify any potential issues that may arise.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
        {
            "code": "DSS_CALCULATION_SUPERVISION_TAB_OVERVIEW_TWO",
            "message": "At the National level, the dashboard displays the number of times the checklist has been allotted and filled by the supervisors across the country. At the Provincial level, the dashboard shows the same information but only for the province in question. At the District level, the dashboard displays the number of times the checklist has been allotted and filled by the supervisors for the district.",
            "module": "rainmaker-hcm-dss",
            "locale": "en_MZ"
        },
